BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-203290@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260925T180000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260925T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260925T193000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat\; Behind the Curtain - To Kill a Mockingbird
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 6 spots left\nSt
 atus: You are Confirmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/event
 s/203290\n\n6:00PM Reception\, 6:30PM Discussion\nExperience a behind-the
 -curtain look as The Huntington Theatre Company prepares to present the f
 irst regional production of Aaron Sorkin’s acclaimed adaptation of To K
 ill a Mockingbird. Artistic Director and Director of the production\, Lore
 tta Greco joins fellow members of the production to explore the art and co
 mplexity of bringing Harper Lee’s enduring classic to the stage\, revea
 ling what audiences rarely see: the journey from script to stage\, the art
 istic decisions made along the way\, and the collaboration required to bri
 ng a production of this scale to life. Together\, they will consider the 
 delicate balance between honoring a story that has resonated for generatio
 ns and embracing the creative freedom and fresh perspective that come with
  a new interpretation.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for me
 mbers only. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be served. We 
 kindly ask that all cancellations be made at least 24 hours prior to the s
 tart of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/203290
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
