BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-203291@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260927T164500Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260927T164500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260927T193000
SUMMARY:Sunday Screening: "Pretty Dirty"
LOCATION:The Muse
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 1 spot left\nSta
 tus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/203291\
 n\n4:45PM Doors Open\, 5:00PM Screening\, 7:15PM Q&A\nGlamorous\, provocat
 ive\, and unapologetically unflinching\, Marilyn Minter has spent nearly f
 ive decades pushing the boundaries of contemporary art. In this Sunday Scr
 eening\, filmmaker Amanda Benchley turns the lens on the trailblazing fem
 inist artist - moving between biography\, studio practice\, and cultural h
 istory - to trace Minter’s rise through New York’s art world\, the c
 ontroversies her work sparked within feminist discourse\, and the enduring
  influence of her lush\, subversive imagery. Fast-paced\, stylish\, and 
 punctuated by notable cameos\, the film offers an intimate portrait of 
 an artistwho has continually challenged convention while embracing pleasur
 e\, beauty\, and desire as forms of power.\n\nFollowing the screening\, me
 mbers are invited to stay for an intimate talkback with visionary filmmake
 r Amanda Benchley and Marilyn Minter herself. Together\, they will pull b
 ack the curtain on the making of the film\, Minter’s extraordinary care
 er\, and the ideas and experiences that have shaped both her art and the f
 ilm.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Theatr
 e fare and refreshments will be served. We kindly ask that all cancellatio
 ns be made at least 24 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/203291
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
