BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-203633@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260930T183000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260930T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260930T200000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: How Hip-Hop Built an Empire
LOCATION:The Muse
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nStatus: You are Confirmed\nEve
 nt URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/203633\n\n6:30PM Reception
 \, 7:00PM Discussion\n\nWhat is it about hip-hop that has transformed gene
 rations of artists into some of the world’s most influential entrepreneu
 rs\, tastemakers\, and cultural forces? Join us for a ’Quin Chat explori
 ng the evolution of the hip-hop artist from performer to mogul - and how a
  genre born from creative expression has become a powerful engine for busi
 ness\, innovation\, and cultural influence. From fashion and record labels
  to food and beverage\, technology\, media\, and beyond\, the conversation
  will examine how artists have built expansive ecosystems around their cre
 ativity while reshaping the industries they enter. \n\nNeil Martinez Belk
 in\, New York Times bestselling author\, will be joined in conversation 
 by Boston native Dart Adams\, an acclaimed journalist\, historian\, resear
 cher\, lecturer\, and author. Together\, they will explore the entreprene
 urial mindset behind hip-hop’s most influential figures\, the relationsh
 ip between cultural credibility and commercial success\, and how the genre
  continues to redefine what it means to be an artist\, and a mogul\, today
 .\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Complimen
 tary light bites and refreshments will be served. We kindly ask that all c
 ancellations be made at least 24 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/203633
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-203637@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261002T173000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261002T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261002T190000
SUMMARY:The Root of Wellbeing with Wildsmith Skin 
LOCATION:The Terrace
DESCRIPTION:Category: Health & Wellness\nPrice: Free\nStatus: Waitlist Only
 \nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/203637\n\n5:30PM Rece
 ption\, 6:00PM Discussion\n\nDiscover the root of wellbeing with Wildsmith
  Skin and an intimate\, immersive evening exploring the powerful role bota
 nicals can play in how we sleep\, restore\, and feel each day. Led by Hale
 y Carr\, Vice President of Operations & Training at Wildsmith Skin\, the c
 onversation will explore the foundations of wellbeing and the importance o
 f our circadian rhythm in supporting sleep quality\, gut and skin health\,
  relaxation\, and mental focus.\n\nWith more than 20 years of experience a
 cross the luxury spa\, wellness\, and hospitality industries\, Haley bring
 s together expertise in aromatherapy\, skin health\, therapeutic touch\, a
 nd holistic wellbeing. Throughout the evening\, members will discover the 
 science and traditions behind Wildsmith’s botanical ingredients while ex
 periencing a selection of the brand’s products firsthand through their t
 extures\, scents\, and formulations.\n\nThe experience extends beyond the 
 conversation to dedicated one on one time with Haley\, offering each membe
 r personalized wellbeing guidance tailored to their lifestyle\, daily rout
 ine\, and individual needs. Leave with a deeper understanding of your own 
 wellness rituals—and simple\, achievable ways to incorporate botanicals 
 and thoughtful practices into everyday life.\n\n*This event is complimenta
 ry and reserved for members only. Complimentary light bites and refreshmen
 ts will be served. We kindly ask that all cancellations be made at least 2
 4 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/203637
CATEGORIES:Health & Wellness
END:VEVENT
